proof_text:
Take $p=q=2$ and let $\mathbf x,\mathbf y\in\ell^2$. For each $N$, Cauchy-Schwarz gives
$$\sum_{n=0}^{N}|x_ny_n|\le
\left(\sum_{n=0}^{N}|x_n|^2\right)^{1/2}
\left(\sum_{n=0}^{N}|y_n|^2\right)^{1/2}
\le \|\mathbf x\|_2\|\mathbf y\|_2.$$
Let $N\to\infty$ to obtain absolute summability and the claimed bound.
